---
import BookingStatus from '../../components/BookingStatus.astro';
import BlueprintLayout from '../../layouts/BlueprintLayout.astro';
---

<BlueprintLayout title="Performance Journal | Forge Rehab & Performance" description="A warm editorial journal of Forge Rehab & Performance's one-on-one Recover, Build, Perform approach." currentPage="home">
  <section class="journal-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div class="journal-hero__copy">
      <p class="folio">Performance journal / Northern New Jersey</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Recovery is a starting point, not the finish line.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Forge Rehab &amp; Performance provides one-on-one, evidence-based physical therapy that progresses with your goals, from understanding the problem to building capacity for what matters next.</p>
      <div class="journal-actions"><BookingStatus /><a class="text-link" href="/concept-02/approach/">Read the Forge Approach</a></div>
    </div>
    <figure class="journal-hero__figure">
      <img src="/assets/forward-court.webp" width="1600" height="1200" fetchpriority="high" alt="A basketball player moves with the ball on an outdoor court" />
      <figcaption>Licensed demo stock. Does not depict Forge patients or people, clinicians or staff, facilities, treatment, or outcomes.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="evidence-folio journal-section" aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
    <header class="section-heading"><p class="folio">Evidence folio / 01</p><h2 id="evidence-title">A clear premise, grounded in individual care.</h2></header>
    <div class="evidence-folio__notes">
      <article><span>Care model</span><strong>One-on-one</strong><p>One clinician, one person, and a progression shaped around the goal.</p></article>
      <article><span>Clinical direction</span><strong>Evidence-based</strong><p>Evaluation, explanation, and progression remain connected throughout care.</p></article>
      <article><span>Working premise</span><strong>Build forward</strong><p>Symptom reduction is part of the work, not the entire destination.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="audience-grid journal-section" aria-labelledby="audience-title">
    <div class="margin-note"><span>Who this is for</span><p>Recognition without categories that box people in.</p></div>
    <div class="audience-grid__body">
      <p class="folio">Field notes / 02</p><h2 id="audience-title">For people whose goals extend beyond feeling less pain.</h2>
      <ul class="audience-grid__list" aria-label="Forge audiences"><li>Active adults</li><li>Athletes</li><li>Weekend warriors</li><li>Strength and fitness enthusiasts</li></ul>
      <p class="large-copy">Different histories. Different demands. A shared desire for a disciplined path back toward meaningful activity.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stage-journal journal-section" aria-labelledby="stages-title">
    <header class="section-heading"><p class="folio">Progression / 03–05</p><h2 id="stages-title">A progression built to keep moving forward.</h2><p>Each stage informs the next. The sequence adapts around individual goals rather than a fixed template.</p></header>
    <ol class="stage-journal__list">
      <li><span>01</span><div><p class="folio">Recover</p><h3>Begin with clarity.</h3><p>Evaluation and understanding establish the foundation. Symptom reduction is part of the work, not the entire destination.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>02</span><div><p class="folio">Build</p><h3>Develop capacity.</h3><p>Strength, mobility, control, capacity, and confidence are progressed in relation to the person and the goal.</p></div></li>
      <li><span>03</span><div><p class="folio">Perform</p><h3>Meet the demand.</h3><p>The process advances toward the demands of chosen activities without treating readiness as a one-size-fits-all benchmark.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="practitioner journal-section" aria-labelledby="practitioner-title">
    <figure><img src="/assets/forward-movement.webp" width="714" height="960" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Two runners stand at starting blocks on an outdoor track" /><figcaption>Licensed demo stock. Does not depict Forge patients or people, clinicians or staff, facilities, treatment, or outcomes.</figcaption></figure>
    <div class="practitioner__body"><p class="folio">Practitioner note / 06</p><h2 id="practitioner-title">Clinical direction from Brandon Coveney, PT, DPT, OCS.</h2><p>Brandon is an orthopedic physical therapist and a 2018 graduate of Sacred Heart University's Doctor of Physical Therapy program, with ties to Northern New Jersey.</p><blockquote>Evidence-based. Progressive. Built around the person in front of you.</blockquote></div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing journal-section" aria-labelledby="closing-title">
    <div><p class="folio">Continue reading / 07</p><h2 id="closing-title">Start with the full approach.</h2><p>Read how Recover, Build, and Perform work together, then return when online scheduling is ready.</p></div>
    <div class="journal-actions"><a class="text-link" href="/concept-02/approach/">Read the Forge Approach</a><BookingStatus /></div>
  </section>
</BlueprintLayout>
